315 0 obj
  << /ActualText (\042Rem\042 units \050root em\051 are based on the root font size defined in our style sheet\056 This means that each element within our system is proportional to the base font size\056 By using \042rem\042\054 we ensure greater consistency and ease of updating in design\056\nAdvantages of \042rem\042 Units\072\nScalability\072 By simply adjusting the base font size\054 we can proportionally adjust all element sizes in the design without manually tweaking each individual element\056\nImproved Accessibility\072 \042Rem\042 units allow for greater accessibility as users can customize the text size according to their needs without compromising readability or the design\047s appearance\056\nConsistency Maintenance\072 By using a single unit of measurement for dimensions\054 we maintain greater consistency in the overall design of the platform\056)
     /K [ 7 ]
     /P 316 0 R
     /Pg 308 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

316 0 obj
  << /K [ 6 315 0 R ]
     /P 319 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 308 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

317 0 obj
  << /ActualText (By using \042rem\042 units\054 we reduce reliance on pixels and simplify the design management and update process\056 Control over the base font size becomes crucial as it impacts all element sizes in our system\056)
     /K [ 9 ]
     /P 318 0 R
     /Pg 308 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

